{#
  ★★ THE STANDING RULE FOR EVERY BLOCK IN THIS FOLDER (user, 2026-09-08):
  ENFORCE, DO NOT NEGATE.

      wrong: "you cannot remove this device if you don't have the key"
      right: "this device can only be removed with the proper key and will
              stay on otherwise"

  The user's reasoning, and it matches what 0792 recorded back in August ("LLM
  do really bad with negative, make them focus on what not to do and end up
  doing it"): a prohibition still puts the forbidden thing in the model's
  context, described in detail, and a model that has just read a vivid
  description of clean dialogue is more likely to write clean dialogue.

  HOW THIS WAS APPLIED, so the pattern is reusable:
    * "Do NOT write intelligible dialogue"  -> "EVERY line she gives is pure
      vocalisation" - say what the output IS, not what it must avoid.
    * "Do NOT have her recognise a person by sight" -> "everything she knows
      about the room arrives through hearing, touch, smell and memory" - give
      the channel that IS open and the closed one needs no mention.
    * "she cannot use her hands" -> "her hands are held out of use" - the same
      fact as a state of the body rather than a missing ability.
    * "It does not come off on its own" -> "It stays exactly as it was put on
      ... time is on the device's side."

  ⚠ AUDITED TO ZERO on 2026-09-08: no "do not / never / cannot / can not /
  no longer" survives in the RENDERED prose of any of the nine blocks. Comments
  like this one are exempt - they are read by people, not by the model.
  Re-run the check before shipping a prompt edit; it is trivial to regress.
#}
{#
  ★★ RENUMBERED 0917 -> 0890 ON 2026-09-08, AND THE NUMBER IS THE POINT.
  The user, after reading a live request: "DEVICES CURRENTLY WORN BY Sofia is
  after her current sense deprivation device. It's better to have it before -
  tell her what she is wearing, than tell Sofia what her current restriction
  are."
  So the WORN list now renders BEFORE every state block (0910 restraint, 0915
  blind, 0916 deaf, 0940 gag): the objects first, then what they take away.
  ⚠ Do not renumber this back above 0900 without that ruling being reversed.
#}
{#
  VRTE DD/ZaZ AddOn - devices currently worn, and how they feel by now.
                                                            (2026-08-26)

  User: "make it a tab in final_instruction like 'device currently worn and
  effect' and follow up with the list of device worn, small description and
  currently how long they been in it and how it feel."

  ── WHERE THE TEXT COMES FROM ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  The whole block is built in VRTE_DDZaZ.dll and arrives as ONE string. That is
  deliberate: SkyrimNet pre-computes every Papyrus decorator for every nearby
  entity on every render cycle, so walking her worn armor in Papyrus - or worse,
  in Jinja - would multiply by actors AND by cycles. The DLL walks it once.

  ── WHAT IS IN IT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  One line per device: what it is, how long it has been on, and the physical
  state that follows from that. Three things drive the wording:

    * CLASS      what the thing does to the body (an armbinder holds the arms
                 folded behind the back; a ring gag holds the mouth open)
    * MATERIAL   read off the device's own NAME, which is where DD and every
                 content mod actually encode it - iron, ebonite, rusted, and
                 the soulgem ladder from a faint prickle up to a black gem
                 pulling at her own magicka
    * DURATION   a real clock in GAME hours, running from when it went on

  ── THE STRAIN CURVE, AND ITS LIMITS ───────────────────────────────────────
  Devices that hold a joint under load - the armbinder family, yokes, pet
  suits, ballet boots - accumulate strain on a five-phase curve. Plain wrist and
  ankle cuffs do NOT: they chafe and ache and stop there, permanently, because
  a pair of cuffs can be worn for days without harm. Gags, blindfolds, plugs and
  piercings have no strain curve at all - they get a sensation line instead.
  Nothing here escalates a device beyond what it physically does.

  ⚠ THE ONE RULE WORTH READING TWICE, and the DLL appends it only when it can
    apply: at the last phase the REPORTED pain FALLS while the harm is greatest,
    because sensation itself is failing. A falling complaint is not improvement.
    It is stated in the block itself rather than here so it travels with the
    state it describes.

  ⚠ Guarded with isString, never `!= ""`: an empty Papyrus decorator result
    arrives as an empty JSON object `{}`, and `{} != ""` is TRUE. That bug put
    two blocks on every NPC in the game for a session (report 23 §32).

  ⚠ Renders in EVERY mode, thoughts included. What is locked on her body and how
    long it has been there is a fact she is aware of; suppressing it in thoughts
    mode would have her think as though her own body were not involved.

  ⚠ Neutral throughout. Every line reports mechanism and sensation - what the
    device does and what the body feels. Never fear, shame, arousal, need or
    resignation. How any of it lands is hers to play.
#}
{% if exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") %}
{# ★ 1.3.0 (2026-09-14): STATE FILE FIRST, decorator as the fallback. VRTE_DDZaZ.dll writes
   Data/SKSE/Plugins/VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state.json the instant a device goes on or off, a name
   arrives, a restraint is released; read_json re-reads on the file's mtime and the random second
   argument defeats SkyrimNet's 55 s callback cache (VRTouchEvents' recipe, VR-verified, report 45).
   Matched on the SkyrimNet entity UUID. No entry for her = the old decorator path, unchanged. #}
{% set _ds = read_json("VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state", random * 10000 + random * 100 + random) %}
{% set _de = 0 %}
{% if isObject(_ds) and existsIn(_ds, "npcs") %}{% for _e in _ds.npcs %}{% if _e.uuid == npc.UUID %}{% set _de = _e %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if isObject(_de) and existsIn(_de, "worn") %}{% set _vd_worn = _de.worn %}{% else %}{% set _vd_worn = vrtedd_worn_devices(npc.UUID) %}{% endif %}
{% if isString(_vd_worn) and _vd_worn != "" %}
{% set _p = "he" %}{% set _pp = "his" %}
{% if decnpc(npc.UUID).isFemale %}{% set _p = "she" %}{% set _pp = "her" %}{% endif %}
**DEVICES CURRENTLY WORN BY {{ decnpc(npc.UUID).name }}.** These are locked on {{ _pp }} body right now. Each line gives the device, how long it has been on, and what {{ _p }} physically feels from it at this point.

{{ _vd_worn }}
Treat all of it as ongoing bodily fact. {{ _p | capitalize }} is LIVING in it: it colours {{ _pp }} posture, {{ _pp }} movement and where {{ _pp }} attention goes, in every line, whether or not {{ _p }} mentions it. Let it reach {{ _pp }} speech where it would naturally come up, and let it shape {{ _pp }} body language everywhere else.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
